# Claude Code settings — BOTH files, deliberately.
#
# settings.local.json was always machine-local. settings.json is nominally the shared/team
# file and used to be tracked, but in practice the tool AUTO-WRITES permission grants into it
# as they are approved, and those grants embed absolute paths — `C:\Users\<name>\...` and
# `additionalDirectories` entries. It has therefore leaked a username into a commit twice:
# once swept in by a `git add -A` that ran after the release privacy scan, and again while
# fixing that, because the file had regenerated in between.
#
# A file that rewrites itself with local paths cannot be a shared file, whatever it is called.
# If a genuinely shared, path-free team config is ever wanted, add it under another name and
# keep it hand-edited.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json

# Stray docker-pull output from interactive sessions
pull_*.log
